pupils return to english schools on  tuesday after the christmas break and  the head teacher at richard challen a  school in south west london is worrying  about staff absences i've had four staff  email me saying they'll be in isolation  and beginning a term now we can manage  that but if that becomes 10 staff or 12  staff we've got huge problems and not  for the first time in the pandemic  english schools are implementing last  minute policy directives from the  government all high school students must  now wear masks in classrooms i like all  the other head teachers around the  country found out about when masking  classrooms for lessons when we read the  national newspapers on sunday morning  which is appalling in my view how is it  that the press know what is going to go  on in the classroom before her teachers  have even been briefed on that but this  is the only real tweak to boris  johnson's omicron gamble while scotland  wales and northern ireland all brought  in restrictions before christmas the  prime minister chose not to for england  he's sticking with his decision  the wayfall for the country as a whole  is to continue with the path that we're  on the gamble is that vaccine coverage  and omicron's relative mildness will  prevent the health service from being  overwhelmed but even boris johnson  recognizes it's not looking good  the pressure on our nhs on our hospitals  is going to be  considerable in the course the next  couple of weeks and maybe more because  as there's no question omicron continues  to to surge through the country  elsewhere in europe with the new year  come new steps france is going ahead  with measures announced last week a  three-day work from home rule for those  who can big public gatherings limited  for three weeks and parliament is  debating a change to france's health  past only the vaccinated would be  allowed in restaurants cafes and more  the health minister condemned alleged  death threats from anti-vaccination  activists  let us not lose sight of the fact that  the objective of this law is not to  restrict individual and collective  liberties of french people the objective  of this law is to save lives it is to  protect our hospitals and relieve the  workload of our health workers  despite opposition from some politicians  the backing of several parties means the  lower house will likely pass the bill  rory helens al jazeera
 

